Use Caskrun's managed Wine 11 client surface for DXMT D3D12 presentation.

Applies to public DXMT e94c312f5c054263acf261cfa109edf13e757587 after
 dxmt-e94c312f-wine-11-win-data.patch and
 dxmt-e94c312f-wine-11-client-surface.patch. Requires the matching original
wine-11.0-dxmt-client-surface.patch already used by the reviewed runtime.

Borrow the swapchain-owned opaque surface through the private D3D12
queue method and prepare it while mutex_commit_ serializes presentation,
immediately before layer synchronization and drawable encoding. This is
the D3D12 equivalent of the existing D3D11 queued PrepareMetalView call.
The queue never retains or asynchronously stores the opaque context;
no public COM method or Wine/Winemetal export changes.

Offered under DXMT's LGPL-2.1-or-later terms.

